      "math_academy_id": "e-9980",
      "problem": "Simplify $\\sqrt{50u^7}.$",
      "worked_solution": "We first write $50u^7$ as the product $25u^6\\cdot 2u$ which contains a perfect square $(25u^6){:}$ \n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\\sqrt{50u^7}&=\\[3pt]\n\t\\sqrt{25u^6\\cdot 2u}&\n\t}\n$$\n\nThen, we separate the product into two separate radicals:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\\sqrt{25u^6\\cdot 2u}&=\\[3pt]\n\t\\sqrt{\\left(5u^3\\right)^2\\cdot 2u}&=\\[3pt]\n\t\\sqrt{\\left(5u^3\\right)^2}\\cdot\\sqrt{2u}&\n\t}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify the radical containing the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\\sqrt{\\left(5u^3\\right)^2}\\cdot\\sqrt{2u}&=\\[3pt]\n\t|5u^3|\\cdot\\sqrt{2u}&=\\[3pt]\n\t|5|\\cdot |u^3|\\cdot\\sqrt{2u}&=\\[3pt]\n\t5|u|^3 \\sqrt{2u}\n\t}\n$$",
